{"$schema":"https://docs.harness.design/files/harness/schema/v0.9.json","$docs":"https://docs.harness.design/files/harness/editing-guide.md","version":0.9,"lengthUnit":"mm","connectors":[{"id":"cl_c11","label":"OEM cluster connector C11","schematicPosition":{"x":620,"y":0},"layoutPosition":{"x":620,"y":0},"width":270,"cavities":[{"id":"c2","designation":"2","signal":"Turn L (G-B) - flasher LH stub"},{"id":"c11","designation":"11","signal":"Turn R (G-Y) - flasher RH stub"},{"id":"c12","designation":"12","signal":"High beam (R-L) - body residual feed"}]},{"id":"cl_c12","label":"OEM cluster connector C12","schematicPosition":{"x":620,"y":338},"layoutPosition":{"x":620,"y":338},"width":270,"cavities":[{"id":"c1","designation":"1","signal":"Park brake (R-G) - grounds via OEM P1 / B2"},{"id":"c8","designation":"8","signal":"Alt L (Y) - charge-lamp drive"},{"id":"c9","designation":"9","signal":"IG +12 (B-O) - charge LED anode side"}]},{"id":"led_board","label":"Cluster LED indicator board","schematicPosition":{"x":620,"y":676},"layoutPosition":{"x":620,"y":676},"width":210,"cavities":[{"id":"hb","designation":"HB","signal":"High beam LED"},{"id":"tl","designation":"TL","signal":"Turn L LED"},{"id":"tr","designation":"TR","signal":"Turn R LED"},{"id":"pk","designation":"PK","signal":"Park brake LED"},{"id":"chg_a","designation":"CHG+","signal":"Charge LED anode, IG side"},{"id":"chg_k","designation":"CHG-","signal":"Charge LED cathode, to alternator L"},{"id":"oil_k","designation":"OIL-","signal":"Oil LED cathode, sunk by the CSB low-side"}]},{"id":"dm_csb_ls","label":"CSB-LS","schematicPosition":{"x":1080,"y":0},"width":150,"cavities":[{"id":"c1","designation":"1","signal":"CSB low-side out - dummy, owned by CAN loom"}],"layoutPosition":{"x":1080,"y":0}}],"wires":[{"id":"w_led_hb","color":"Red","source":{"id":"cl_c11","handle":"c12"},"target":{"id":"led_board","handle":"hb"}},{"id":"w_led_tl","color":"Green","source":{"id":"cl_c11","handle":"c2"},"target":{"id":"led_board","handle":"tl"}},{"id":"w_led_tr","color":"Green","source":{"id":"cl_c11","handle":"c11"},"target":{"id":"led_board","handle":"tr"}},{"id":"w_led_pk","color":"Red","source":{"id":"cl_c12","handle":"c1"},"target":{"id":"led_board","handle":"pk"}},{"id":"w_led_chg_ig","color":"Black","source":{"id":"cl_c12","handle":"c9"},"target":{"id":"led_board","handle":"chg_a"}},{"id":"w_led_chg_l","color":"Yellow","source":{"id":"led_board","handle":"chg_k"},"target":{"id":"cl_c12","handle":"c8"}},{"id":"w_led_oil","color":"White","source":{"id":"dm_csb_ls","handle":"c1"},"target":{"id":"led_board","handle":"oil_k"}}],"schematicNotes":[{"id":"n_src","schematicPosition":{"x":0,"y":-1400},"width":390,"text":"ST185 cluster LED loom. A separate circuit from the cluster itself - warning and status indicators only. Migrated 2026-09-19 from docs/electrical/CLUSTER-LED-DIAGRAM.html, which was the only record of these connections."},{"id":"n_stripe","schematicPosition":{"x":0,"y":-1140},"width":390,"text":"Stripe colours live in the cavity text - the schema colour list has no striped values. C11-2 G-B, C11-11 G-Y, C11-12 R-L, C12-1 R-G, C12-8 Y, C12-9 B-O."},{"id":"n_chg","schematicPosition":{"x":0,"y":-880},"width":390,"text":"Charge LED is a series path: IG +12 (C12-9) to LED to alternator L (C12-8). ON when the regulator grounds L (not charging), OFF when L sits near battery volts. Alternator S is a battery sense line, NOT a lamp - do not wire it here."},{"id":"n_oil","schematicPosition":{"x":0,"y":-620},"width":390,"text":"Oil LED is CAN-driven, no discrete sense wire. Link sets Low Oil Press 2 on 0x3F1 bit4; PCLink packs the CSB low-side on 0x643. The CSB sinks the cathode; the anode goes to +12 IG."},{"id":"n_open","schematicPosition":{"x":0,"y":-360},"width":390,"text":"NOT YET DETERMINED - do not build until settled. 1) The common ground or return for the high beam, turn L and turn R LEDs; the source diagram does not state it. 2) Whether the LED board carries its own current-limiting resistors or the loom must. 3) The oil LED anode feed (+12 IG) - stated as existing but no pin given. Park brake grounds through the OEM P1 / B2 path, so it needs no return here."}]}